Z||000022||batboy||02-21-2001||10:17 PM||||I'm batty...not nutty!<P>I was stationed at Iceland years ago, thanks to the US Air Farce. After one winter night of being on duty and watching a particularly amazing display of northern lights (aurora borealis), I went to the base library and studied up on it. A couple nights later, my drinking buddies and I were popping barley pop tops when the discussion turned to how beautiful the northern lights had been lately. One fellow wondered out loud what caused them and I ripped off a long winded technical explanation. There was a lengthy pause and the guy said, "Thank you for the lecture, Professor!" Feeling silly from the beer, we all burst out laughing our butts off. I had to live with the "Professor" nickname for weeks.<P>My mind is full of all kinds of useless trivia, like peanuts aren't really nuts. Trouble is, it crowds out all the important stuff I should be remembering instead. LOL!||||reg||1
