Z||000028||Phil||02-22-2001||09:18 AM||||A bunch of years ago a woman in our town died in a resturant from eating a bowl of chili. The secret ingredient was a dab of peanut butter, there was a big law suit because the resturant didn't warn of peanuts. Also a friend of mine developed a reaction to peanuts overnight, he never had any trouble with peanuts for over 30 yrs then one day he had a snickers bar and almost died. Now we call him Skippy (I have wierd friends)||||reg||1
Z||000029||frontal lobe||02-22-2001||10:13 AM||||A lot of people have SERIOUS reactions to peanuts, and peanut OIL is in a lot of products, too.  So the food industry is pretty particular about listing that as a possible ingredient.<P>You would think, though, that when you buy a jar of peanuts that you would ASSUME it contained peanuts.  But for legal purposes, that's what our country has come to.<P>I knew peanuts were a legume and not a nut.  But that doesn't mean I'm going to BOIL them and eat them, goober.  Anyone tried them?  Yuk.  I'll take mine roasted, thanks.||||reg||1
